{"content_hash": "48ae357c3704a31c", "version_id": 575, "article_id": 58, "level_code": "en_c1", "lang": "en", "level": 5, "level_label": "C1 高级", "title": "Nikon strips scientist of prize after AI-generated microscope video", "title_zh": "尼康撤销科学家奖项，获奖显微镜视频被证实为AI生成", "has_translation": true, "topic": "tech", "source": "bbc_tech", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cr86z33pdy9vo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1614036417651-efe5912149d8?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8MXx8cHJpemUlMjB3aW5uaW5nJTIwaW1hZ2V8ZW58MHwwfHx8MTc5MTc2NTYxNXww&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Brands&People on Unsplash", "author": "Brands&People", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@brandsandpeople?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/yellow-paper-award-ribbon-ZdqSuxl3Lak?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(16, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(54, 46%, 48%)", "label": "TECH", "seed": "cec84960fed8"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-12", "word_count": 226, "reading_minutes": 1.1, "lead": "Nikon has disqualified the winner of its prestigious Small World In Motion competition after concluding that the winning video was generated using artificial intelligence, a decision that has ignited a fierce debate over authenticity in scientific imaging.", "lead_zh": "尼康已取消其著名的“小世界动态”摄影大赛冠军的资格，认定获奖视频系人工智能生成。这一决定引发了关于科学影像真实性的激烈争论。", "preview": "The firm announced that the entry by Dr Ning Xu of Tsinghua University breached competition rules prohibiting generative AI. The video purpo", "preview_zh": "该公司宣布，清华大学徐宁博士的参赛作品违反了禁止使用生成式AI的比赛规则。该视频声称展示了纤毛——微小的毛发状结构——在患有呼吸道疾病PCD的儿童气道中运动。尼康强调，取消资格并非对徐博士的职业声誉或科学贡献的评判，并表示将审查比赛规则和程序。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 563, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/58/en_c1.mp3", "duration": 96.25, "size_bytes": 581184, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 260, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@870ce8b/content/data/versions/575.json", "paragraphs": ["The firm announced that the entry by Dr Ning Xu of Tsinghua University breached competition rules prohibiting generative AI. The video purported to show cilia—tiny hair-like structures—moving in the airway of a child with the respiratory condition PCD. Nikon stressed that the disqualification was not a judgment on Xu's professional reputation or scientific contributions, and said it would review the contest's rules and procedures.", "The decision followed a thorough re-evaluation of the video and supporting materials, alongside consultations with the judging panel. Concerns had been raised by several scientists, including former judges, who complained on Nikon's LinkedIn page that the footage appeared inauthentic. Xu acknowledged using AI but maintained he had acted within the rules and cooperated fully with the investigation.", "Dr Robert Hirst, a scientist at the University of Leicester, said he was 'not surprised' and 'knew immediately that the video was fabricated.' With two decades of experience diagnosing PCD, he noted that the cells and cilia 'look nothing like those from PCD patients.' He added that the controversy has affected patients, scientists, doctors and support networks worldwide.", "The incident has cast a spotlight on the growing use of AI in scientific imagery, raising questions about how competitions can verify authenticity. Nikon, which has run the contest for 15 years, now faces pressure to tighten its rules. The BBC has approached Dr Xu for comment."], "paragraphs_zh": ["该公司宣布，清华大学徐宁博士的参赛作品违反了禁止使用生成式AI的比赛规则。该视频声称展示了纤毛——微小的毛发状结构——在患有呼吸道疾病PCD的儿童气道中运动。尼康强调，取消资格并非对徐博士的职业声誉或科学贡献的评判，并表示将审查比赛规则和程序。", "这一决定是在对视频及辅助材料进行彻底重新评估并与评审团协商后作出的。此前，包括前评委在内的多位科学家提出了担忧，他们在尼康的LinkedIn页面上投诉称视频似乎不真实。徐博士承认使用了AI，但坚称自己遵守了规则，并全力配合了调查。", "莱斯特大学的罗伯特·赫斯特博士表示他“并不惊讶”，并且“立刻就知道视频是伪造的”。凭借二十年诊断PCD的经验，他指出这些细胞和纤毛“看起来与PCD患者的完全不同”。他还补充说，这一争议已影响到全球的患者、科学家、医生和支持网络。", "该事件使人们关注AI在科学影像中日益广泛的使用，引发了关于竞赛如何验证真实性的质疑。已举办该赛事15年的尼康，如今面临收紧规则的压力。BBC已联系徐博士寻求置评。"], "body": "The firm announced that the entry by Dr Ning Xu of Tsinghua University breached competition rules prohibiting generative AI. The video purported to show cilia—tiny hair-like structures—moving in the airway of a child with the respiratory condition PCD. Nikon stressed that the disqualification was not a judgment on Xu's professional reputation or scientific contributions, and said it would review the contest's rules and procedures.\n\nThe decision followed a thorough re-evaluation of the video and supporting materials, alongside consultations with the judging panel. Concerns had been raised by several scientists, including former judges, who complained on Nikon's LinkedIn page that the footage appeared inauthentic. Xu acknowledged using AI but maintained he had acted within the rules and cooperated fully with the investigation.\n\nDr Robert Hirst, a scientist at the University of Leicester, said he was 'not surprised' and 'knew immediately that the video was fabricated.' With two decades of experience diagnosing PCD, he noted that the cells and cilia 'look nothing like those from PCD patients.' He added that the controversy has affected patients, scientists, doctors and support networks worldwide.\n\nThe incident has cast a spotlight on the growing use of AI in scientific imagery, raising questions about how competitions can verify authenticity. Nikon, which has run the contest for 15 years, now faces pressure to tighten its rules. The BBC has approached Dr Xu for comment.", "body_zh": "该公司宣布，清华大学徐宁博士的参赛作品违反了禁止使用生成式AI的比赛规则。该视频声称展示了纤毛——微小的毛发状结构——在患有呼吸道疾病PCD的儿童气道中运动。尼康强调，取消资格并非对徐博士的职业声誉或科学贡献的评判，并表示将审查比赛规则和程序。\n\n这一决定是在对视频及辅助材料进行彻底重新评估并与评审团协商后作出的。此前，包括前评委在内的多位科学家提出了担忧，他们在尼康的LinkedIn页面上投诉称视频似乎不真实。徐博士承认使用了AI，但坚称自己遵守了规则，并全力配合了调查。\n\n莱斯特大学的罗伯特·赫斯特博士表示他“并不惊讶”，并且“立刻就知道视频是伪造的”。凭借二十年诊断PCD的经验，他指出这些细胞和纤毛“看起来与PCD患者的完全不同”。他还补充说，这一争议已影响到全球的患者、科学家、医生和支持网络。\n\n该事件使人们关注AI在科学影像中日益广泛的使用，引发了关于竞赛如何验证真实性的质疑。已举办该赛事15年的尼康，如今面临收紧规则的压力。BBC已联系徐博士寻求置评。", "text": "The firm announced that the entry by Dr Ning Xu of Tsinghua University breached competition rules prohibiting generative AI. The video purported to show cilia—tiny hair-like structures—moving in the airway of a child with the respiratory condition PCD. Nikon stressed that the disqualification was not a judgment on Xu's professional reputation or scientific contributions, and said it would review the contest's rules and procedures. The decision followed a thorough re-evaluation of the video and supporting materials, alongside consultations with the judging panel. Concerns had been raised by several scientists, including former judges, who complained on Nikon's LinkedIn page that the footage appeared inauthentic. Xu acknowledged using AI but maintained he had acted within the rules and cooperated fully with the investigation. Dr Robert Hirst, a scientist at the University of Leicester, said he was 'not surprised' and 'knew immediately that the video was fabricated.' With two decades of experience diagnosing PCD, he noted that the cells and cilia 'look nothing like those from PCD patients.' He added that the controversy has affected patients, scientists, doctors and support networks worldwide. The incident has cast a spotlight on the growing use of AI in scientific imagery, raising questions about how competitions can verify authenticity. Nikon, which has run the contest for 15 years, now faces pressure to tighten its rules. The BBC has approached Dr Xu for comment.", "vocab": [{"word": "disqualify", "pos": "verb", "zh": "取消资格", "note": "常与 from 连用，如 disqualify sb from a competition", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "prestigious", "pos": "adj", "zh": "有声望的，著名的", "note": "用于形容奖项、机构等", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "generative AI", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "生成式人工智能", "note": "指能生成文本、图像等内容的AI", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "breach", "pos": "verb", "zh": "违反，破坏", "note": "比 break 更正式，常与 rules, contract 搭配", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "purport", "pos": "verb", "zh": "声称，自称", "note": "常与 to do 连用，暗示可能不真实", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "cilia", "pos": "noun", "zh": "纤毛", "note": "生物学名词，单数形式为 cilium", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "respiratory", "pos": "adj", "zh": "呼吸的", "note": "如 respiratory disease 呼吸道疾病", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "inauthentic", "pos": "adj", "zh": "不真实的，假的", "note": "反义词 authentic", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "fabricate", "pos": "verb", "zh": "伪造，捏造", "note": "常指编造信息或证据", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "controversy", "pos": "noun", "zh": "争议，争论", "note": "常与 spark, ignite 等动词搭配", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "cast a spotlight on", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "使……成为焦点", "note": "比喻用法，引起关注", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "authenticity", "pos": "noun", "zh": "真实性", "note": "形容词为 authentic", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "tighten", "pos": "verb", "zh": "收紧，加强", "note": "如 tighten rules 收紧规则", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "approach", "pos": "verb", "zh": "联系，接洽", "note": "指向某人寻求信息或帮助", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "Prize-winning image which sparked backlash was AI-generated, Nikon rules", "summary_original": "The camera-maker says it is now re-evaluating the rules and procedures of its Small World in Motion contest.", "body_original": "Prize-winning image which sparked backlash was AI-generated, Nikon rules\nBy\nZoe Kleinman\nTechnology & AI editor\nPublished\n9 October 2026\nThe winner of a prestigious scientific photography competition has been disqualified following concerns raised by other scientists that it was fake.\nNikon said the use of generative AI in the composition of the video broke the rules of its Small World In Motion contest, which accepts photos and video taken using powerful microscopes.\nThe firm said the video \"did not comply with the competition rules regarding generative AI\", but added it was not a judgement of the entrant's professional reputation or scientific contributions.\nIt said it would now look at the rules and procedures of the annual contest, which has been running for 15 years and is specifically for microscopic images.\nNikon said it came to the decision \"after thoroughly re-evaluating the video and supporting materials and consulting with members of our judging panel\".\nThe winning entry came from Dr Ning Xu, from Tsinghua University in China, who submitted a short video showing tiny, hair-like structures called cilia moving in the airway of a child with the respiratory condition PCD.\nThe BBC has approached him for comment.\nA number of scientists, including former competition judges, complained to Nikon on its LinkedIn page that the video did not appear to be real.\nXu had acknowledged using AI, but said he believed he had acted within the rules, and had cooperated with Nikon's investigation.\nUniversity of Leicester scientist Dr Robert Hirst, who was among the first experts to voice concerns, said he was \"not surprised\" and he \"knew immediately that the video was fabricated\".\n\"I have been diagnosing PCD for 20 years by examining their cilia waveform, length, cell size and shape,\" he said.\nHirst, who is lead scientist for the NHS centre for PCD diagnosis at the university, said the cells and cilia \"look nothing like those from PCD patients\".\n\"This controversy has impacted a lot of patients, scientists, doctors and PCD support networks around the world,\" he said.\nTiny image sparks big backlash in Nikon photo contest\nPublished\n1 October\nWhat is AI, how does it work and why are some people concerned about it?\nPublished\n14 September\nSign up for our Tech Decoded newsletter\nto follow the world's top tech stories and trends.\nOutside the UK? Sign up here\n.\nRelated topics\nArtificial intelligence\nPhotography\nScience & Environment", "